messages:
lee: Follow-up on the session-controller decomposition RFC. Proposal: split the monolithic session-controller into four orthogonal modules: persistence (durable store), router (request affinity + sharding), policy (lifecycle + TTLs), and telemetry (metrics/tracing). goal is independent release cycles and fewer cross-service synchronous calls.

alex: which module do we tackle first? persistence seems risky but gives the biggest win for scale.

tara: +1 persistence first, but we should also extract router logic simultaneously to avoid having a single new bottleneck. do staged extraction: persistence + router -> policy -> telemetry.

jin: migration concerns: schema changes for session blobs, backward compatibility, and live upgrades. need explicit on-disk versioning and a read-compat shim for 3 months.

infra-sre: resource isolation note: session-controller currently consumes burst CPU during large rehydrates. if we split, each module needs explicit CPU and memory QoS. recommend per-module resource classes and p99 CPU throttling tests.

lee: suggested IPC contract is gRPC with a small versioned payload. example proto for session record:

```proto
syntax = "proto3";
package redwood.session.v1;

message SessionRecordV1 {
  string id = 1;
  map<string, bytes> kv = 2;
  int64 last_active_ms = 3;
  int32 schema_version = 4; // bump for non-backward compatible changes
}

service SessionPersistence {
  rpc Get(SessionGetRequest) returns (SessionRecordV1) {}
  rpc Put(SessionRecordV1) returns (google.protobuf.Empty) {}
}
```

alex: using map<string, bytes> addresses earlier evolution concerns. please add optional metadata map for hints (owner, ttl_policy).

tara: rollout plan idea: feature-flagged path at the router layer. keep old monolith path as fallback. start with internal traffic + e2e tests, then 1% public, then 10%, etc.

jin: tests to add: live migration test that reads old-format session then writes new-format and verifies client behavior; conflict/reconcile tests for near-simultaneous writes.

infra-sre: alerts/dashboard: add per-module error rate, p50/p95/p99 latency, and a synthesized session-consistency check (sample sessions compared between new pipeline and legacy for divergence).

lee: compatibility approach: on Get, if schema_version unknown -> forward to monolith persistence path and increment metric. add circuit-breaker so fallback can't overload legacy.

qa-bot: ci pipeline triggered: ci/session-decomp/feature-branch -> unit + integration + chaos tests.

alex: ops/rollback: feature toggle off + scale down new modules + pause routing switch. document steps in runbook and add runbook link in PR.

tara: timeline proposal: proto + contracts (1 week), persistence impl + compatibility shim (2 weeks), router extraction + canary infra (1 week), policy + telemetry extraction + perf testing (2 weeks), ramp and postmortem (1 week) -> ~7 weeks.

lee: action owners: alex: proto & contracts; jin: compatibility shims + migration tests; infra-sre: perf harness + dashboards; tara: rollout orchestration & runbook; qa-bot/qa: add chaos scenarios. I'll coordinate cross-team sync.

alex: will open PR with contract doc and link this thread.

lee: thanks everyone. we'll review constraints in next architecture sync and lock down the experiement window.
